About the shopkeepers' names:
The source code indicates that the current shopkeepers' names are
grouped by nationality: Indonesian for food shops, Dutch for jewelers,
etc.  The obvious choice for restaurants as you describe them would be
French; for the barbershop, Figaro comes to mind, which would make it
either Spanish or Italian, depending on whether you go by the location
of his shop or the language he sings.  Although it would be interesting
if one of the barber names was Sweeny...
Ah well.  I'm not sure this is such a good plan.  The charm of the
shopkeepers' names as they stand is that, to English-speakers anyway,
they are all odd-looking and difficult to place.



